[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_solsc")
fish_name = "Druyip Man o' War"
grade = 3
sprite = ExtResource("2_324cw")
catch_blurb = "Back from the trenches."
description = "The Man o' War is the only known genus found thriving across so many separate galaxies. Their genetic similarity suggests they once shared a home, which is believed to be none other than the supermassive form of Alcedo Atthis. Their transparent, gas-filled “hats” keep them floating near the surface, and their 30-foot-long, stinging tentacles prevent the passage of organisms of any size. Thus, a popular theory among the Pwaaga is that they were once components of Alcedo Atthis’ immune system, but many scientists still question if she even existed.

Because Man o’ War are colonial creatures, it is a rite of passage for many budding biologists to analyze the small organisms that a Man o’ War is composed of. This exercise sheds light on the subtle differences in fundamental biology across different galaxies. However, because their tentacles can paralyze, injure, or kill those who come into contact with them, it is also considered the most stressful part of the field. A young intern by the name of Marvin once said, “I would rather wrangle a Swordfish.”

On planets with an atmosphere, Man o’ War are pushed by the sail-like protrusions on their heads. However, Druyip* Man o’ War are often found with sailor hats** and weighted medals. These accessories appear to keep the Men o’ War in place by blocking their sails and weighing them down. After observing F.I.S.H.E. officials placing these accessories on the Man o’ War, locals have started to theorize that the corporation is exploiting this species’ impenetrable defenses to protect their “trade-secrets-in-a-bottle.” However, no one has managed to break through their formation—some believe they are simply protecting their young.

*Druyip is the original, “dated” name for Pollywood. 
**A few incidents report sentient behavior from these sailor hats. There is no clear theory on why.
"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://cr3nmjdvpgh0a"
